<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Landlibell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1511</span> · Also known as Landlibell of 1511</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Landlibell was a charter issued by Emperor Maximilian I in 1511 that set out the defence obligations of the Tyrolean estates. It required the estates and districts to raise fixed contingents of troops for the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a>, while exempting them from service outside it. It remained the basis of the Tyrolean militia, the Schützen, into the 19th century.</p></div>
